# Build context filter for server/app/api-gateway/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile's dev and prod stages both do `COPY . .` after `pnpm install`.
# Without this file that copy sweeps in whatever happens to be sitting in a
# developer's checkout, and two of those are actively harmful rather than
# merely wasteful:
#
#   - .env  — a real credential, baked into an image layer. dotenv does not
#     override variables already in the process environment, so it does not
#     change how the container runs; it just travels with the image forever.
#   - node_modules — installed on the *host*. `COPY . .` lands after the
#     `pnpm install` layer, so a host tree silently replaces the one built
#     inside node:24-alpine. Any package with a native binding (musl vs glibc,
#     a different CPU) then fails at runtime rather than at build time.
#
# The root .dockerignore does NOT cover this build. It applies to the `web`
# image, which is the only one whose context is the repository root.
#
# NOT excluded, on purpose: src/prisma/generated/. The Prisma 7 `prisma-client`
# generator writes the client into the source tree (prisma/schema.prisma,
# `output = "../src/prisma/generated"`) and it is committed. Nothing in the
# Dockerfile runs `prisma generate`, so excluding it would break `nest build`
# on an unresolved import.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
dist
coverage

.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode

# Test fixtures and specs are not needed at runtime, but `nest build` type-checks
# against tsconfig, so leaving test/ in is cheaper than debugging a path error.
# Only the throwaway output is dropped.
.eslintcache
*.log
.DS_Store
